CORE dfcc-only
valid.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract-rec f
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: SUCCESS$
^\[f\.precondition\.\d+\] line 1 Check requires clause of contract contract::f for function f: SUCCESS$
^\[f\.assertion\.1\] .*base case is reachable: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^\s*ASSUME ¬\(overflow-\*\(cast\(4, unsignedbv\[64\]\), 4\)\)
^warning: ignoring
--
A recursive call replaced by the contract asserts the generated static-array
requires clause and satisfies it. The top-level contract check does not assume
that clause; the minimum is checked at the call to the wrapped implementation.
The reachability assertion is the only failure, so the check is not vacuous.
